From 4c1f0f6b9b0d5f7e2a3c4d5e6f708192a3b4c5d6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mehdi Zibaoui <mehdi@zibaoui.dev>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 14:10:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] media: amlogic: amvdec: h264: free the parser scratch buffer

codec_h264_stop() frees every coherent buffer it allocated, but not
h264->scan_copy, the cached copy of the current access unit that
meson_amvdec_codec_h264_scan_copy() allocates with kvmalloc(). The core
then frees the codec private data with kfree(sess->priv), so the pointer
is lost and the buffer is never released.

For a 1080p stream the OUTPUT plane is 4 MiB, which kvmalloc() serves
through kmalloc_order(): the pages are charged to NR_SLAB_UNRECLAIMABLE
without belonging to any visible slab cache. Every playback session
therefore lifts Slab/SUnreclaim by ~4 MiB while /proc/slabinfo, vmalloc
and the per-cgroup accounting stay flat, and neither stopping Kodi nor
unloading the module returns the memory.

Release the scratch buffer before the core drops the private data.
kvfree() accepts a NULL pointer, so partially initialised sessions are
covered too.
---
 drivers/media/platform/amlogic/amvdec/codec_h264.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/amlogic/amvdec/codec_h264.c b/drivers/media/platform/amlogic/amvdec/codec_h264.c
--- a/drivers/media/platform/amlogic/amvdec/codec_h264.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/amlogic/amvdec/codec_h264.c
@@ -1663,6 +1663,11 @@
 					  h264->colocate_vaddr[i],
 					  h264->colocate_paddr[i]);
 
+	/* The core frees the private data right after this callback. */
+	kvfree(h264->scan_copy);
+	h264->scan_copy = NULL;
+	h264->scan_copy_size = 0;
+
 	return 0;
 }
